Findings:
Pre-execution SQL self-review and independent review found local PL/pgSQL variable names colliding with visible columns; new locals were renamed to req_* names before any SQL run. Root also caught the mechanical rename of the authority JSON fingerprint key; the literal was restored before execution. Complete corrected SQL and transport review found no remaining source blocker.
The first primary transport run passed 90/90 and independent compatibility passed 2/2. The first actual SQL run passed 71/72: the deleted-thread administrative fixture retained its saved snapshot while setting deleted_at, violating the unchanged P3b deletion constraint before reaching the reader. The fixture now clears saved_snapshot and saved_at as required. No SQL constraint or implementation assertion was weakened. Three additional absent-clock unsafe/null cases verify the new explicit guard; the corrected expanded SQL suite passes 75/75. Initial TypeScript also identified a malformed-client test cast requiring an explicit unknown intermediate; only that test annotation was corrected. Initial diagnostics remain preserved.
Final aggregate checks pass on frozen source. The reader can observe an older unexpired issuance with fresh shorter Auth without renewing either deadline, works before target claim creation, and preserves all lifecycle/accounting records. Full/peeled protocol-2 replies remain incompatible with the unchanged old verifier. The next concrete dependency is a separate v2 crypto/current-evidence verifier, followed later by owned orchestration and coordinated cutover.

